**Decision: AVOID** (conviction 2/5 — below the min-4 buy threshold)

The screen's mechanical pullback filters are technically satisfied (50-day proximity, intact 50d>200d trend, neutral RSI, positive 6m/12m relative strength, 2:1 reward:risk, 3.1x resistance room), but three things keep conviction below the buy bar: (1) the "pullback" was actually a ~59% peak-to-trough crash (Jun high 2,189,000 → Aug low 901,000) in seven weeks — not a shallow dip, so the 50-day proximity looks coincidental rather than a controlled setup; (2) earnings quality is weak — TTM net margin 94.3%/ROE 84.9% convert to only ~1% FCF conversion, so the "cheap" 4.2x P/E is a non-cash accounting artifact, not a valuation cushion, while P/FCF (361x) and P/B (2.5x) are both above the stock's own 5-year max; (3) no genuine catalyst — headlines are routine filing notices only, and the required ~28% move to target must occur within ~33 days (before Nov 13 earnings) on a beta-2.44, 5.6%-ATR name, raising gap-through-stop risk.

